{% from "components/icons.njk" import icon, socialLink %}
{#- Contact card ("Let's design a better product experience."), the same on every page:
    the homepage (inside "Working across time zones"), every case study and the All work page.
    Styles: .cpanel / .cwin in home.css and work.css (keep the two in step).

    Before including it, `{% set contactHeading = "h2" %}` where the card starts its own section
    (case studies, All work); the homepage leaves it at h3, under its "Working across time zones" h2.
    The heading has id="contact-h" for the section's aria-labelledby.

    Text on the left; the watercolor window sits in the third column, above the divider (wide screens only),
    with an "Artistic Creations: Coming Soon" note beside it and a hand-drawn arrow rising from the window to it.
    The window is layered so contact-window.js can animate it: shutters closed until the card is scrolled to,
    then they swing open and the arrow flies out of the window to point at the note; scrolling back up reverses it.
    Layers, bottom to top: the window with its shutters painted out, the two shutters, the plants and vine
    that stay in front of them, and the untouched painting (shown whenever the window is open). #}
{%- set contactTag = contactHeading or "h3" %}
<div class="cpanel" id="contact">
  <div class="cpanel__intro">
    <div class="cpanel__text">
      <{{ contactTag }} class="cpanel__title" id="contact-h">Let’s design a better product experience.</{{ contactTag }}>
      <p class="cpanel__sub">
        I’m open to on-site/remote product design roles and thoughtful collaborations. If you’re working on a
        product that needs clearer flows, stronger interfaces, or a more considered design approach,
        I’d like to hear about it.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="cpanel__aside">
      <div class="cpanel__art cwin" aria-hidden="true">
        {%- for layer in ["base", "shutter-l", "shutter-r", "front"] %}
        <img class="cwin__{{ layer }}" src="{{ ('/assets/images/contact-window-' + layer + '.webp') | rel }}" alt="" width="240" height="240" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        {%- endfor %}
        <img class="cwin__painting" src="{{ '/assets/images/contact-window.webp' | rel }}" alt="" width="240" height="240" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
      </div>
      <p class="cpanel__soon">
        <span class="cpanel__soon-kicker">Artistic Creations:</span>
        <span class="cpanel__soon-label">Coming Soon</span>
        {% include "svg/contact-arrow.svg" %}
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="cpanel__cols">
    <div>
      <p class="cpanel__label">Email:</p>
      <a class="cpanel__mail" href="mailto:{{ site.email }}"><span class="btn__icon">{{ icon("mail") }}</span>{{ site.email }}</a>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="cpanel__label">Resume:</p>
      <a class="cpanel__mail cpanel__dl" href="{{ site.resume | rel }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        {#- #}<span>Download Resume</span><span class="btn__icon">{{ icon("arrow-up-right") }}</span><span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span>
      {#- #}</a>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="cpanel__label">I know you want to follow, so:</p>
      <ul class="cpanel__social">
        {%- for link in site.social %}
        <li style="--i: {{ loop.index0 }}">{{ socialLink(link.name, link.url) }}</li>
        {%- endfor %}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
<script defer src="{{ '/assets/js/contact-window.js' | rel }}"></script>
